// idiom: grant
// summary: the reach a confined row (one a stack layer adds) may compose against, named by the composition's owner
// rule: `grant @row with { key, ... }` lists keys the row `requires`; only the base composition or the site layer may write it, never a layer for itself
// rule: a grant is reach, not trust: the row stays non-first-party; `with` is required, because `@row {` lexes as a host body
// fill: grant @records with { approvals, writer }

composition Demo {
  row @approvals from "approvals.rvl" provides approvals
  row @writer from "writer.rvl" provides writer
  stack "layers/records.rvl"
  grant @records with { approvals, writer }
}
